  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{20, 20}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"348d5306-6291-42ce-bbaa-2094870b2f31"],

Cell["4. Where space contracts, where space expands", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"187e704a-c62a-428b-b100-67b2191b79b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What does \"contraction in front, expansion behind\" mean operationally?  \
The ADM expansion scalar of the Eulerian observers measures it directly.  An \
Eulerian observer is one that moves with the spatial slices \[LongDash] their \
4-velocity is the unit normal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["n", "\[Mu]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"]}]}], ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "5ba6addd-8535-4595-8c92-be26e36a16d4"],
 ".  The extrinsic curvature of the slice measures how it bends inside \
spacetime as time flows:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fcaf1cd2-9024-4bb9-a24e-6ff7209e4e71"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["K", 
    RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["1", 
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Alpha]"}]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["D", "i"], " ", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "j"]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["D", "j"], " ", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
        RowBox[{"i", "j"}]]}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"3f990df9-6ff7-4acd-bd5b-11c2d296f8fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["D", "i"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "956d4fae-cdf6-4c55-be44-ff73d8d49370"],
 " the spatial covariant derivative on the slice (compatible with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
    RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "bc4c8735-32d2-42c9-9525-3c22958ef50d"],
 ").  Its trace is the volume expansion rate seen by Eulerian observers:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05d3943d-bb87-4b30-8332-cb20a3ec538a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox["K", 
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}]]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SubscriptBox["D", "i"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"5cd80891-69da-4310-b82c-f50dd1be4e0a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For Alcubierre's metric ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "=", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "70f6c939-ee09-4adc-94dc-23982479c7bf"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], "=", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "df986a8d-dd06-476a-9951-8a35fb9ab475"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "i"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "i"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "4fb29f92-1654-4748-ba73-f32697ffa04d"],
 " is just the ordinary divergence.  Plugging in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "x"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubscriptBox["v", "s"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"f", "(", 
      SubscriptBox["r", "s"], ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "500c6c4c-5110-4f9f-a107-38f5e6201769"],
 " and using the chain rule one gets a strikingly clean closed form:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6c37bd6c-6f20-49ad-af43-398ba29e6813"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", "\[Del]", "\[CenterDot]", "\[Beta]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["v", "s"], "(", 
      RowBox[{"x", "-", 
       SubscriptBox["x", "s"]}], ")"}], 
     SubscriptBox["r", "s"]], " ", 
    FractionBox["df", 
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SubscriptBox["r", "s"]}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"e651ab2d-5267-4536-b19e-92714b6c03f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For Alcubierre's bubble it's antisymmetric in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "-", 
    SubscriptBox["x", "s"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "1e8856d3-0009-4b23-ad6f-1137075f6668"],
 ": positive (volume expansion) behind the bubble, negative (volume \
contraction) in front, zero on the y-z plane through the centre.  Plotted on \
a slice at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"z", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "8a2a21f9-14ef-4c3e-bfa9-053861e553ea"],
 " using a divergent colourmap:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"edc563c3-e01b-4baf-892e-aedb22bc0f97"],

Cell["\<\
DensityPlot[
  AlcubierreExpansionScalar[{1, 1, 8}, {0, x, y, 0}],
  {x, -2.5, 2.5}, {y, -2.5, 2.5},
  PlotPoints -> 220, ColorFunction -> \"RedBlueTones\",
  PlotLegends -> Automatic,
  Epilog -> {Black, Thick, Circle[{0, 0}, 1]}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"9690b964-0a20-414d-ab25-f83efa786ec3"],

