    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"Figure 6. A regular Cartesian grid distorted by the \
Alcubierre shift field as the bubble sweeps from left to right.  The colour \
shows the shift magnitude.  Inside the bubble all four points of any small \
grid cell move together \[LongDash] no internal stretching, no tidal forces.  \
All the deformation is concentrated in the wall.\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->720]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{20, 20}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"30d97d08-9673-446c-a10e-3d5841d378d7"],

Cell["7. Geodesics: getting swept up by a warp bubble", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"92c2afcd-f517-4637-9e8b-d45335b942a9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Drop a population of test particles into the spacetime and let them follow \
geodesics.  Free-fall trajectories ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"], "(", "\[Lambda]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "78a68946-c2e8-4782-9047-85df6f292837"],
 " obey the geodesic equation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05e69bb6-23df-4edb-957d-0db9f18a45b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["d", "2"], 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"]}], 
    RowBox[{"d", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "2"]}]], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Mu]"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Alpha]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Beta]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"]}], "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"20d60190-66d8-49cd-8e85-f4575fcb9e3e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "which we rewrite as a first-order ODE system for position and 4-velocity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"d", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"], "/", "d\[Lambda]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "d2a9f7b1-7b08-4360-9a4e-75c1816d36bc"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6415f374-88b4-4eea-9d28-9aad0edb2697"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"]}], ",", 
   "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Mu]"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Alpha]"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Beta]"]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",\

 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"4c4ae606-4d40-4396-b927-69a2673a3982"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For massive (timelike) particles the affine parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Lambda]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7dde0d-215f-469b-84fb-3a8239ff4740"],
 " can be chosen to be the proper time, and the velocity is normalised so that"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00c0d438-eb48-4abd-b87a-a4fb1c573dc2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["g", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Nu]"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"ed2c6e86-b612-4917-8773-950db14b868b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For light rays (null geodesics) the normalisation becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["g", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["k", "\[Mu]"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["k", "\[Nu]"], "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "42f1d6c2-a996-4047-a4c6-fb485eab74f6"],
 " instead, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Lambda]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "cffcc08f-057f-4b69-a132-d900f3e44041"],
 " is no longer proper time (which is zero for a photon) but any affine \
parameter along the ray.  The Christoffel coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "de74af79-f65c-4233-91c5-80936e363968"],
 " in the right-hand side are the same expressions Wolfram generated \
symbolically in Section 3 \[LongDash] we just substitute the current ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "0878122a-354f-4d52-bfed-af8a6bbac180"],
 " values into them and hand the result to ",
 StyleBox["NDSolve", "Input"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"24fe14de-267c-4132-8a7d-19feaade9e06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In ADM language an Eulerian observer (the analogue of a stationary one in \
flat space) has spatial 3-velocity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "72131bb1-23ca-43b7-83f1-a50b09c823ae"],
 ", so as the bubble approaches a stationary particle from the left, the \
particle is grabbed by the shift field and accelerated forward; as the bubble \
passes, the particle decelerates back to rest.  Particles further from the \
axis feel proportionally less of the bubble's grip:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bcd83960-3c58-4115-8a34-f789244b4618"],

Cell["\<\
alcShift[t_, x_, y_] := -1.0 TanhShape[Sqrt[(x - 1.0 t)^2 + y^2], 1, 8];

(* Eulerian advection: dx/dt = -beta^x = +alcShift.
   Use a fixed Euler step dt set by the time grid spacing. *)
sweep[{x0_, y0_}, ts_] := With[{dt = ts[[2]] - ts[[1]]},
  FoldList[
    {#1[[1]] + dt alcShift[#2, #1[[1]], y0], #1[[2]]} &,
    {x0, y0}, Rest[ts]]];

ts = Range[0., 4., 0.05];
trajs = Table[sweep[{-3., y0}, ts], {y0, Range[-1.4, 1.4, 0.35]}];
ListAnimate @ Table[
  Show[DensityPlot[Abs[alcShift[ts[[k]], x, y]], {x, -3, 5.5},
                   {y, -2, 2}, PlotPoints -> 90,
                   ColorFunction -> \"BlueGreenYellow\"],
       Graphics[{Black, Thick, Line /@ (Take[#, k] & /@ trajs),
         Red, PointSize[0.022], Point /@ (#[[k]] & /@ trajs)}]],
  {k, 1, Length[ts], 2}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"c57a6568-5cc8-48c2-8a76-8c77611d264e"],

